\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0   The covenant of my baptism,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj  was made to place me in The Lord;
\par  The Father, Son and Holy Spirit
\par  that represents the fertile land
\par  that I was planted that I may grow
\par  and flourish and bring forth the good fruit.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2.   The heaven'ly Father made me His son,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj   a new covenant he has made.
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj O, my Lord, gracefully prepare me
\par As your own son whose heart is yours
\par The whole of my being and of my soul
\par and my spirit for you Lord evermore.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   3.  And who soever shall believe it,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 and also be baptized in you
\par shall ever have life everlasting,
\par and would not ever lose his life,
\par My Lord, let me be a believer
\par \pard     as your son, and you as my Father.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

